   "design": "Configure slot-based sign-up in the parent app of the pupil records system ({OTHER}): the teacher checks the activity post with slots and posts it once, parents pick a slot, the checked reminder goes out the day before, and open slots show on the teacher's list. A short instruction card per activity type in {DOCS} goes with the reminder, so the in-class briefing is shorter.",
   "previous_blocker": "Volunteer requests ran through chat threads and a paper list, so tracking replies took repeated messages.",
   "enabler_now": "Parent apps support sign-up slots and reminders as standard features.",
   "still_hard": "Some parents never use the app, and a good activity depends on how the teacher guides helpers in the moment.",
   "human_edge": "Making volunteers and older pupils feel useful and steering complex play so every child takes part.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "serve_new_group",
    "what": "Parents who work irregular hours and can now pick a slot that fits, instead of answering a group chat in time."
   },
   "altitude": "Nothing changes in decision rights; less chasing of replies.",
   "reach": [
    {
     "role": "preschool teacher",
     "task": "Organise parent help for play activities",
     "learn": "Whether the same sign-up slots work for younger children's groups."
    }
   ],
   "build_days": {
    "coding": "0-1",
    "integration": "0-1",
    "testing_rollout": "1-2",
    "consent_and_access": "1-3"
   },
   "run_cost": "none",
   "evidence": [
    {
     "claim": "A Dutch pupil records system comes with a parent app.",
     "grade": "E2",
     "source": "[S4]",
     "kind": "capability"
    },
    {
     "claim": "Parent apps can offer sign-up slots and reminders.",
     "grade": "E1",
     "source": "model knowledge",
     "kind": "capability"
    },
    {
     "claim": "Regular volunteers working with children may need a certificate of conduct under national rules; parent contact data falls under GDPR.",
     "grade": "E1",
     "source": "model knowledge",
     "kind": "legal"
    }
   ],
   "assumptions": [
    "Boundary: from planning the activity to guiding it; the activity's content is outside.",
    "Input contract: parent contact details and class membership, produced by the school administration in the pupil records system; slots per activity set by the teacher in s2; fallback is the class chat.",
    "Parent and colleague time is outside the teacher's savings.",
    "Guiding the activity is unchanged.",
    "Parents' replies are shown in s3 at share 1. Preparing the post keeps 60 of s2; checking and posting it keep their full time."
   ],
   "unknowns": [
    "Whether the school's parent app has sign-up slots.",
    "How many activities per term need helpers."
   ],
   "research_questions": [
    "Does slot sign-up reach parents who did not volunteer before?"
   ],
